-- title:
--   Transition maps for the twisted Tate tower of height h+hₑ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, the ideal $(p)$ is maximal, and $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete; let $\Phi$ be a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$ (i.e. $d$ power series in $2d$ variables with vanishing constant term, identity linear terms, associative, with $\Phi(Y,X)=\Phi(X,Y)$), and let $h,h_e$ be natural numbers. The data are: a tower $(E_v)_{v\in\mathbb{N}}$ of commutative rings that are cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, with surjective bialgebra maps $st_v\colon E_{v+1}\to E_v$, $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}E_v=p^{v h_e}$ and $\ker st_v$ equal to the image of the augmentation ideal of $E_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity; a transition-compatible family $c_2^{(v)}\in (E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}E_v)^d$ with entries in $p(E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}E_v)$; and power defects $C_{v,n}\in (E_v)^d$ with entries in $pE_v$, killed by the counit, compatible with the $st_v$, and satisfying $C_{v,p^vm}=[m]_\Phi(C_{v,p^v})$ in the sense of $(p)$-adic evaluation of `Φ.nthSeries m` at $C_{v,p^v}$. Further, a tower $(L_v)$ of commutative rings that are cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, finite free over $\mathcal{O}$ of rank $p^{vh}\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}E_v$, together with bialgebra maps $\iota_v\colon E_v\to L_v$, algebra maps $\Psi_v\colon \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to L_v$ and surjective algebra maps $\theta_v\colon E_v[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to L_v$ with $\theta_v\circ C=\iota_v$, $\theta_v(X_i)=\Psi_v(X_i)$ and $\ker\theta_v$ generated by the $d$ series $[p^v]_\Phi(X)_i-C\bigl([{-1}]_\Phi\text{-evaluation of }C_{v,p^v}\bigr)$ (the image of `Φ.nthSeries (p^v)` in $E_v[[X]]$ minus the constant obtained by $(p)$-adically evaluating `Φ.invSeries` at $C_{v,p^v}$); it is assumed that each $\Psi_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $pL_v$, that $\Psi_v$ is given by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the $\Psi_v(X_i)$, that the counit kills $\Psi_v(X_i)$, that $E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}\mathcal{O}[[X]]\to L_v$ induced by $\iota_v$ and $\Psi_v$ is surjective, that the comultiplication of $\Psi_v(X_i)$ is $\Phi\bigl(\Psi_v(X)\otimes 1,\;\Phi(1\otimes\Psi_v(X),(\iota_v\otimes\iota_v)c_2^{(v)})\bigr)$, and that the $n$-fold convolution power of the identity sends $\Psi_v(X_i)$ to $\Phi\bigl([n]_\Phi(\Psi_v(X)),\iota_v(C_{v,n})\bigr)$, all in the relevant $(p)$-adic evaluations. The conclusion asserts the existence of bialgebra maps $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$ that are surjective, satisfy $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}L_v=p^{v(h+h_e)}$, have $\ker t_v$ equal to the image of the augmentation ideal of $L_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity, and satisfy $t_v\circ\iota_{v+1}=\iota_v\circ st_v$ and $t_v\circ\Psi_{v+1}=\Psi_v$.
--
--   This supplies exactly the transition data required by the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): from an étale tower of height $h_e$ and a level-by-level presentation of a formal-group twist of height $h$, it produces compatible surjections whose kernels are the $p^v$-torsion ideals, so that the twisted Tate tower $(L_v)$ has height $h+h_e$. It is used by [`MvFormalGroup.exists_pDivisibleTower_of_cocycle`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_pDivisibleTower_of_cocycle), which assembles the tower into a $p$-divisible group.
-- source:
